## Vercel Speed Insights Implementation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the email spam classifier project.

### What was implemented:

**Modified:**
- `mini pro 1/email-spam-classifier/frontend/index.html` - Added Vercel Speed Insights integration

### Implementation details:

1. **Fetched latest documentation** from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart to ensure using the most up-to-date installation steps

2. **Identified framework**: This is a vanilla HTML/CSS/JavaScript project served by Flask backend, with no build system or package.json

3. **Implementation approach**: Used the CDN-based approach recommended for vanilla HTML projects:
   - Added a module script that imports `injectSpeedInsights` from the official CDN
   - Called `injectSpeedInsights()` to initialize performance monitoring
   - Placed the script in the `<head>` section after the font imports

4. **Code added**:
   ```html
   <!-- Vercel Speed Insights -->
   <script type="module">
   import { injectSpeedInsights } from 'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@vercel/speed-insights@1/dist/index.mjs';
   injectSpeedInsights();
   </script>
   ```

### Why this approach:

- For vanilla HTML projects without a build system, the CDN approach is the recommended method
- No npm package installation needed since there's no package.json in the project
- The `@vercel/speed-insights@1` package is loaded directly from CDN
- This implementation automatically begins collecting Web Vitals metrics (LCP, FID, CLS, TTFB) when the page loads

### Verification:

✅ HTML syntax validated successfully
✅ No build errors (static HTML project)
✅ Code follows the official Vercel documentation patterns
✅ Preserves all existing functionality

### Next steps:

Once deployed to Vercel:
1. The Speed Insights will automatically start collecting performance data
2. Metrics will be visible in the Vercel dashboard under the Speed Insights tab
3. No additional configuration required

The implementation is production-ready and will start tracking performance metrics immediately upon deployment.
